                            {
                              "key": "degradedIsAmber",
                              "label": "Degraded services turn a card amber"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "section",
                      "title": "Change the rules",
                      "columns": 2,
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "type": "conditional",
                          "when": {
                            "source": {
                              "kind": "stream",
                              "event": "ui",
                              "path": "hintsOn"
                            },
                            "op": "eq",
                            "value": true
                          },
                          "blocks": [
                            {
                              "type": "note",
                              "title": "What each field means",
                              "lines": [
                                "Leave a number empty to use the default. That is why they are text boxes rather than spinners: an empty number field would be sent as zero, which is indistinguishable from somebody meaning zero.",
                                "Machines contacted at once - how many ssh or curl calls run in parallel on the machine you are connected to. Higher is faster and costs it more file descriptors.",
                                "Connect timeout - what an address with nothing at it costs, multiplied by the size of the range.",
                                "Per-machine timeout - the ceiling on one machine's answer. Agent installs raise this by themselves, because downloading and installing is minutes rather than seconds.",
                                "Agent port - where agents are expected. The installer always binds 8741; change this only if something in front of them moves it.",
                                "Pull telemetry every - how often the daily figures are collected. Agents keep their own, so more often than every quarter hour buys nothing.",
                                "First-pull backfill - how far back to reach the first time a machine is collected from. An agent may hold a year; this stops the first pull asking for all of it at once.",
                                "Check host keys - on means every machine must already be in the known_hosts of the account this app connects as. The form sends this box as shown, so the check step warns if saving would turn it off."
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
